From: legentus <129329825+legentus@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] skip the intro movie: PS3_SKIP_INTRO=1 (F2 > Mods > Skip intro movie)

The splash movie (splash_america.bik etc., about 12 s) is the only movie before
the title screen. The game builds its name from the string "splash_%s" at
0x007CDBA8 (EBOOT 1.04); with PS3_SKIP_INTRO=1 its first letter is changed at
load, so the movie it asks for does not exist and the game goes straight to the
title. The string is checked first, so another EBOOT is left alone.

diff --git a/game_patches.cpp b/game_patches.cpp
index de16cf4..c8872e0 100644
--- a/game_patches.cpp
+++ b/game_patches.cpp
@@ -94,8 +94,31 @@ bool apply_one(const std::string& type, uint32_t addr, const std::string& value)
 
 } // namespace
 
+/*
+ * PS3_SKIP_INTRO=1 (F2 > Mods > Skip intro movie): no splash movie at start, the
+ * game goes straight to its title screen. The splash is the only movie before
+ * the title; the game names it from the string "splash_%s" (splash_america.bik,
+ * splash_europe.bik ...). Its first letter is changed, so the movie it asks for
+ * does not exist and the splash ends at once. A data write like the community
+ * patches below, checked against the string first, so another EBOOT is left alone.
+ */
+static void infamous2_skip_intro(void)
+{
+    const char* e = getenv("PS3_SKIP_INTRO");
+    if (!e || e[0] != '1' || !vm_base) return;
+    static const uint32_t kSplashName = 0x007CDBA8u;   /* "splash_%s", EBOOT 1.04 */
+    char* p = (char*)vm_base + kSplashName;
+    if (memcmp(p, "splash_%s", 10) != 0) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "[patch] skip intro: the splash movie's name is not where this EBOOT keeps it; not skipped\n");
+        return;
+    }
+    p[0] = 'x';
+    fprintf(stderr, "[patch] skip intro: the splash movie is skipped (PS3_SKIP_INTRO=1)\n");
+}
+
 extern "C" void infamous2_apply_patches(const char* elf_path)
 {
+    infamous2_skip_intro();
     const char* want_env = getenv("PS3_PATCHES");
     if (!want_env || !*want_env) return;
     std::vector<std::string> want;
